                <pb facs="0345" n="301" xml:id="pg301"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Secretary Acheson traveled to Bonn
                    and Paris, May 23 to 29, 1952 to participate in bilateral, tripartite, and
                    quadripartite negotiations with the Foreign Ministers of the United Kingdom,
                    France, and the Federal Republic of Germany, incident to the signing at Bonn on
                    May 26 of the Convention on General Relations between the Federal Republic and
                    France, the United Kingdom, and the United States, and related conventions, and
                    to the signing at Paris on May 27 of the treaty establishing a European Defense
                    Community and related conventions, protocols, and declarations.</p>
                <p>For documentation on the Secretary’s trip to Bonn for the signing of the various
                    agreements concerning contractual relations, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v07p1">volume VII</ref>; for documentation on his
                    trip to Paris for the signing of the European Defense Community Treaty, see <ref
                        target="#pg571">pages 571</ref> ff. Also see <ref target="#pg675">pages
                        675</ref>–<ref target="#pg688">688</ref> herein.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
